{"title": "Series and Progressions (Level 3)", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The value of 2<sup>2</sup> + 4<sup>2</sup> + 6<sup>2</sup> + .... + 20<sup>2</sup> is equal to:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>2<sup>2</sup> + 4<sup>2</sup> + 6<sup>2</sup> + .... + 20<sup>2</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["1540", "770", "385", "1260"], "options_hi": ["1540", "770", "385", "1260"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>2<sup>2</sup>(1<sup>2</sup>+2<sup>2</sup>+3<sup>2</sup>+...+10<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= 4 x {10(10+1)(2x10+1)/6} (Sum of first n<sup>2</sup> terms)</p><p>= 4x385</p><p>= 1540</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>2<sup>2</sup>(1<sup>2</sup>+2<sup>2</sup>+3<sup>2</sup>+...+10<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= 4 x {10(10+1)(2x10+1)/6} (Sum of first n<sup>2</sup> terms)</p><p>= 4x385</p><p>= 1540</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p></p><div>&nbsp;If &nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">(1 + 3 + 5 + 7.. 20 terms)</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">(2 + 4 + 6 + .. n terms)</span></div>&nbsp; = &nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">40</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">11</span></div>&nbsp;, then find n.&nbsp;</div>", "q_hi": "<p></p><div>&nbsp;If &nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">(1 + 3 + 5 + 7.. 20 terms)</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">(2 + 4 + 6 + .. n terms)</span></div>&nbsp; = &nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">40</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">11</span></div>&nbsp;, then find n.&nbsp;</div>", "options_en": ["7", "10", "8", "9"], "options_hi": ["<p>7</p>", "<p>10</p>", "<p>8</p>", "<p>9</p>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Here the numerator is the sum of first 20 odd numbers which is equal to 20<sup>2</sup> i.e. 400</p><p>Denominator is the sum of first n even numbers which is of the form n<sup>2</sup> + n</p><p>400/(n<sup>2</sup> + n) = 40/11</p><p>On solving we get, n = 10</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here the numerator is the sum of first 20 odd numbers which is equal to 20<sup>2</sup> i.e. 400</p><p>Denominator is the sum of first n even numbers which is of the form n<sup>2</sup> + n</p><p>400/(n<sup>2</sup> + n) = 40/11</p><p>On solving we get, n = 10</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The sum of all three digit numbers divisible by 9 is -</p>", "q_hi": "<p>9 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376; -</p>", "options_en": ["55450", "55430", "55530", "55350"], "options_hi": ["55450", "55430", "55530", "55350"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Required numbers are 108, 117, 126...... 999</p> <p>This is an A.P. in which a = 108, d = 9 and l = 999</p> <p>Let the number of terms = n. </p> <p>So a + (n-1) x d = 999</p> <p>So, n = 100</p> <p>Required sum = n/2(a + l) = 100/2 x (108 + 999) = 55350</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Required numbers are 108, 117, 126...... 999</p> <p>This is an A.P. in which a = 108, d = 9 and l = 999</p> <p>Let the number of terms = n. </p> <p>So a + (n-1) x d = 999</p> <p>So, n = 100</p> <p>Required sum = n/2(a + l) = 100/2 x (108 + 999) = 55350</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The sum (101 + 102 + 103 + ........ + 200) is equal to:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; (101 + 102 + 103 + ........ + 200) &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["15000", "15025", "15050", "15090"], "options_hi": ["15000", "15025", "15050", "15090"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>101 + 102 + 103 + ....... + 200</p> <p>S = (100+1) + (100+2) + (100+3) + ........ + (100+100)</p> <p>S = (100+100+100+.... 100 times) + (1+2+3+ .... +100)</p> <p>S = (100*100) + (1+2+3+ .... +100)</p> <p>S = (10000) + (1+2+3+ .... +100)</p> <p>S = 10000 + 100*(100 + 1)/2 because sum of first 'n' natural numbers = n(n+1)/2</p> <p>S = 10000 + 5050 = 15050</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>101 + 102 + 103 + ....... + 200</p> <p>S = (100+1) + (100+2) + (100+3) + ........ + (100+100)</p> <p>S = (100+100+100+.... 100 times) + (1+2+3+ .... +100)</p> <p>S = (100*100) + (1+2+3+ .... +100)</p> <p>S = (10000) + (1+2+3+ .... +100)</p> <p>S = 10000 + 100*(100 + 1)/2 because sum of first 'n' natural numbers = n(n+1)/2</p> <p>S = 10000 + 5050 = 15050</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of X if X = <img width=275 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image029.png\">.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X = &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;<img width=275 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image029.png\">.</p>", "options_en": ["25420", "22410", "23770", "24250"], "options_hi": ["25420", "22410", "23770", "24250"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=197 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image030.png\"></p><p><img width=220 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image031.png\"></p><p><img width=236 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image032.png\"></p><p><img width=259 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=75 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=360 height=24 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image035.png\"></p><p><img width=232 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=167 height=28 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=120 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=253 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image039.png\">.</p><p><img width=212 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=139 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image041.png\"></p><p><img width=59 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image042.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=197 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image030.png\"></p><p><img width=220 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image031.png\"></p><p><img width=236 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image032.png\"></p><p><img width=259 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=75 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=360 height=24 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image035.png\"></p><p><img width=232 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=167 height=28 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=120 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=253 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image039.png\">.</p><p><img width=212 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=139 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image041.png\"></p><p><img width=59 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19856/image042.png\"></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If sum of n consecutive positive even numbers is 2352, find n.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; n &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 2352 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; n &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["46", "48", "51", "49"], "options_hi": ["46", "48", "51", "49"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of n consecutive even numbers = n(n+1) = 2352</p><p>n<sup>2</sup>+ n  -  2352 = 0</p><p>n<sup>2</sup> + 49n  -  48n  -  2352 = 0</p><p>n = -49 or +48</p><p>Hence, n = <b>48</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of n consecutive even numbers = n(n+1) = 2352</p><p>n<sup>2</sup>+ n  -  2352 = 0</p><p>n<sup>2</sup> + 49n  -  48n  -  2352 = 0</p><p>n = -49 or +48</p><p>Hence, n = <b>48</b></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The 10<sup>th</sup> term of a geometric series is 8 times the 7<sup>th</sup> term of the series. If 5<sup>th</sup> term of the series is 80, then what is the 8<sup>th</sup> term of the series?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 10&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2346;&#2342; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; 7&#2357;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2342; &#2325;&#2366; 8 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 5&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2346;&#2342; 80 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 8&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2346;&#2342; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1280", "320", "640", "2560"], "options_hi": ["1280", "320", "640", "2560"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>The 10<sup>th</sup> term of a geometric series is 8 times the 7<sup>th</sup> term of the series.</p><p>=&gt; ar<sup>9</sup> = 8 * ar<sup>6</sup></p><p>=&gt; r<sup>3</sup> = 8</p><p>=&gt; r = 2</p><p>5<sup>th</sup> term of the series is 80</p><p>=&gt; ar<sup>4</sup> = 80</p><p>=&gt; a * 2<sup>4</sup> = 80</p><p>=&gt; a = 80/16</p><p>=&gt; a = 5</p><p>Hence, 8<sup>th</sup> term of the series = 5 * 2<sup>7</sup> = 640</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The 10<sup>th</sup> term of a geometric series is 8 times the 7<sup>th</sup> term of the series.</p><p>=&gt; ar<sup>9</sup> = 8 * ar<sup>6</sup></p><p>=&gt; r<sup>3</sup> = 8</p><p>=&gt; r = 2</p><p>5<sup>th</sup> term of the series is 80</p><p>=&gt; ar<sup>4</sup> = 80</p><p>=&gt; a * 2<sup>4</sup> = 80</p><p>=&gt; a = 80/16</p><p>=&gt; a = 5</p><p>Hence, 8<sup>th</sup> term of the series = 5 * 2<sup>7</sup> = 640</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of 1/0.9+1/0.09+1/0.009+&#8943; up to 6 terms?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1/0.9+1/0.09+1/0.009+&#8943; &#2325;&#2375; 6 &#2346;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1111110/9", "555555", "999999", "555555/9"], "options_hi": ["1111110/9", "555555", "999999", "555555/9"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Given series is in the form of G.P.:</p><p>Then, first term = a = (1/0.9)</p><p>Common ratio = r = (1/0.09)/(1/0.9) = 10</p><p>Total terms = n = 6</p><p>Therefore, sum = a(r<sup>n</sup>  -  1)/(r  -  1)</p><p>= (1/0.9)(10<sup>6</sup>  -  1)/(10  -  1)</p><p><b>= 1111110/9</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given series is in the form of G.P.:</p><p>Then, first term = a = (1/0.9)</p><p>Common ratio = r = (1/0.09)/(1/0.9) = 10</p><p>Total terms = n = 6</p><p>Therefore, sum = a(r<sup>n</sup>  -  1)/(r  -  1)</p><p>= (1/0.9)(10<sup>6</sup>  -  1)/(10  -  1)</p><p><b>= 1111110/9</b></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>There are two numbers X and Y such that geometric mean of X and Y is four-fifth of the Arithmetic mean of X and Y. What is the ratio of X and Y?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2325;&#2367; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;, X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 4/5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["3: 4", "4: 1", "5: 4", "6: 1"], "options_hi": ["3: 4", "4: 1", "5: 4", "6: 1"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>The geometric mean of X and Y is four-fifth of the Arithmetic mean of X and Y</p><p>=&gt; &radic;XY = (4/5) * (X + Y)/2</p><p>=&gt; (X + Y)/2&radic;XY = 5/4</p><p>By componendo and dividendo rule,</p><p>(X + Y + 2&radic;XY)/(X + Y  -  2&radic;XY) = (5+4)/(5-4)</p><p>=&gt; (&radic;X + &radic;Y)<sup>2</sup>/(&radic;X - &radic;Y)<sup>2</sup> = 9/1</p><p>=&gt; (&radic;X + &radic;Y)/(&radic;X - &radic;Y) = 3</p><p>=&gt; &radic;X + &radic;Y = 3&radic;X - 3&radic;Y</p><p>=&gt; 2&radic;X = 4&radic;Y</p><p>=&gt; &radic;X/&radic;Y = 2</p><p>=&gt; X/Y = 4/1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The geometric mean of X and Y is four-fifth of the Arithmetic mean of X and Y</p><p>=&gt; &radic;XY = (4/5) * (X + Y)/2</p><p>=&gt; (X + Y)/2&radic;XY = 5/4</p><p>By componendo and dividendo rule,</p><p>(X + Y + 2&radic;XY)/(X + Y  -  2&radic;XY) = (5+4)/(5-4)</p><p>=&gt; (&radic;X + &radic;Y)<sup>2</sup>/(&radic;X - &radic;Y)<sup>2</sup> = 9/1</p><p>=&gt; (&radic;X + &radic;Y)/(&radic;X - &radic;Y) = 3</p><p>=&gt; &radic;X + &radic;Y = 3&radic;X - 3&radic;Y</p><p>=&gt; 2&radic;X = 4&radic;Y</p><p>=&gt; &radic;X/&radic;Y = 2</p><p>=&gt; X/Y = 4/1</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the sum of the 4 <sup>th</sup> and the 20 <sup>th</sup> terms of an arithmetic progression equals the sum of the 6 <sup>th</sup> , 12 <sup>th</sup> and 16 <sup>th</sup> terms, which term of the progression is necessarily zero?</p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2339;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2380;&#2341;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2368;&#2360;&#2357;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354;, &#2331;&#2336;&#2375;, &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;&#2361;&#2357;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2360;&#2379;&#2354;&#2361;&#2357;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2342; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2339;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2346;&#2342; &#2309;&#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2340;&#2307; &#2358;&#2370;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["8 <sup>th</sup>", "10 <sup>th</sup>", "11 <sup>th</sup>", "9 <sup>th</sup>"], "options_hi": ["&#2310;&#2336;&#2357;&#2366;&#2305;", "&#2342;&#2360;&#2357;&#2366;&#2305;", "&#2327;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2361;&#2357;&#2366;&#2305;", "&#2344;&#2380;&#2357;&#2366;&#2305;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "\"<p> Let the first term and the common difference be a and d respectively.</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/>\r (a + 3d) + (a + 19d) = (a + 5d) + (a + 11d) + (a + 15d)</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 0 = a + 9d</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/>\r the 10 <sup>th</sup> terms is necessarily zero</p><p></p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> Let the first term and the common difference be a and d respectively.</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/>\r (a + 3d) + (a + 19d) = (a + 5d) + (a + 11d) + (a + 15d)</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 0 = a + 9d</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/>\r the 10 <sup>th</sup> terms is necessarily zero</p><p></p>\""}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;What is the sum of the series&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">6</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">7</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">8</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">36</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">49</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">64</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">216</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">343</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">512</span></div>&nbsp;+ ......&nbsp;</div></p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">6</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">7</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">8</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">36</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">49</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">64</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">216</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">343</span></div>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">512</span></div>&nbsp;+ ......&nbsp;</div></p><p></p>", "options_en": ["107/210", "11/21", "121/210", "11/210"], "options_hi": ["107/210", "11/21", "121/210", "11/210"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The series is (1/6 + 1/36 + 1/216 ...) + (1/7 + 1/49 + 1/343 + ..) + (1/8 + 1/64 + 1/512 + ..)</p><p> = (1/6)/(1 - 1/6) + (1/7) / (1-1/7) + (1/8)/(1-1/8)</p><p>= 1/5 + 1/6 + 1/7 = 107/210</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The series is (1/6 + 1/36 + 1/216 ...) + (1/7 + 1/49 + 1/343 + ..) + (1/8 + 1/64 + 1/512 + ..)</p><p> = (1/6)/(1 - 1/6) + (1/7) / (1-1/7) + (1/8)/(1-1/8)</p><p>= 1/5 + 1/6 + 1/7 = 107/210</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of 4 + 32 + 108 + 256 + ........ + 4n<sup>3</sup>.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>4 + 32 + 108 + 256 + ........ + 4n<sup>3</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["n (n + 1)<sup>2</sup>", "n (n + 1)", "n (n + 1)", "[n (n + 1)]<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["n (n + 1)<sup>2</sup>", "n (n + 1)", "n (n + 1)", "[n (n + 1)]<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>k<sup>th</sup> term = 4k<sup>3</sup></p><p>n<sup>th</sup> term = 4n<sup>3</sup></p><p>Required sum =</p><p><img width=105 height=92 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11154/image004.png\"></p><p>= [n (n + 1)]<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>k<sup>th</sup> term = 4k<sup>3</sup></p><p>n<sup>th</sup> term = 4n<sup>3</sup></p><p>Required sum =</p><p><img width=105 height=92 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11154/image004.png\"></p><p>= [n (n + 1)]<sup>2</sup></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p> If 1 <sup>2</sup> + 2 <sup>2</sup> + 3 <sup>2</sup> + -------- + 10 <sup>2</sup> = 385, then 3 <sup>2</sup> + 6 <sup>2</sup> + 9 <sup>2</sup> + ----- + 30 <sup>2</sup> is equal to </p><p> </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 1 <sup>2</sup> + 2 <sup>2</sup> + 3 <sup>2</sup> + -------- + 10 <sup>2</sup> = 385, &#2340;&#2379; 3 <sup>2</sup> + 6 <sup>2</sup> + 9 <sup>2</sup> + ----- + 30 <sup>2</sup> &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;-</p>", "options_en": ["2310", "3465", "1155", "770"], "options_hi": ["2310", "3465", "1155", "770"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "\"<p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 3 <sup>2</sup> + 6 <sup>2</sup> + 9 <sup>2</sup> + ------- + 30 <sup>2</sup></p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r (3 &#215; 1) <sup>2</sup> + (3 &#215; 2) <sup>2</sup> + (3 &#215; 3) <sup>2</sup> + ------- + (3 &#215; 10) <sup>2</sup></p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 9 [1 <sup>2</sup> + 2 <sup>2</sup> + 3 <sup>2</sup> + ------- + 10 <sup>2</sup> ]</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 9 &#215; 385 </p><p>= 3465</p><p></p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 3 <sup>2</sup> + 6 <sup>2</sup> + 9 <sup>2</sup> + ------- + 30 <sup>2</sup></p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r (3 &#215; 1) <sup>2</sup> + (3 &#215; 2) <sup>2</sup> + (3 &#215; 3) <sup>2</sup> + ------- + (3 &#215; 10) <sup>2</sup></p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 9 [1 <sup>2</sup> + 2 <sup>2</sup> + 3 <sup>2</sup> + ------- + 10 <sup>2</sup> ]</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 9 &#215; 385 </p><p>= 3465</p><p></p>\""}, {"q_en": "<p>If number of terms are equal in both the series given below, then find the last term of the series B.</p><p>Series A: 126, 139, 152,......, 321.</p><p>Series B: 56, 77, 98,....,</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2346;&#2342; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p>&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; A: 126, 139, 152,......, 321.</p><p>&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; B: 56, 77, 98,....,</p>", "options_en": ["371", "350", "329", "308"], "options_hi": ["371", "350", "329", "308"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>For series A: 126, 139, 152,......, 321.</p><p>The following series is in the arithmetic progression, as the difference between every two consecutive terms is same. So,</p><p>a = 126, d = 139  -  126 = 13</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= 321</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= a + (n  -  1)d</p><p>321 = 126 + (n  -  1) x 13</p><p>n = 16</p><p>Now, for series B: 56, 77, 98,....,</p><p>a = 56, d = 77  -  56 = 21</p><p>n = 16</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= a + (n  -  1)d</p><p>= 56 + 15 x 21</p><p>= 371</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>For series A: 126, 139, 152,......, 321.</p><p>The following series is in the arithmetic progression, as the difference between every two consecutive terms is same. So,</p><p>a = 126, d = 139  -  126 = 13</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= 321</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= a + (n  -  1)d</p><p>321 = 126 + (n  -  1) x 13</p><p>n = 16</p><p>Now, for series B: 56, 77, 98,....,</p><p>a = 56, d = 77  -  56 = 21</p><p>n = 16</p><p>a<sub>n </sub>= a + (n  -  1)d</p><p>= 56 + 15 x 21</p><p>= 371</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of 6<sup>3</sup> + 8<sup>3</sup> + 10<sup>3</sup> + 12<sup>3</sup> + ... + 20<sup>3</sup>?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>6<sup>3</sup> + 8<sup>3</sup> + 10<sup>3</sup> + 12<sup>3</sup> + ... + 20<sup>3 </sup>&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["21448", "24418", "24128", "24818"], "options_hi": ["21448", "24418", "24128", "24818"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>We know that,</p><p>Sum of cube of first n numbers = [n(n+1)/2]<sup>2</sup></p><p>6<sup>3</sup> + 8<sup>3</sup> + 10<sup>3</sup> + 12<sup>3</sup> + ... + 20<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 2<sup>3</sup> * (3<sup>3</sup> + 4<sup>3</sup> + 5<sup>3</sup> + .. + 10<sup>3</sup>)</p><p>= 8 * [(1<sup>3</sup> + 2<sup>3</sup> + 3<sup>3</sup> + .. + 10<sup>3</sup>)  -  (1<sup>3</sup> + 2<sup>3</sup>)]</p><p>= 8 * [(10 * 11/2)<sup>2</sup>  -  (2 * 3/2)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= 8 * [3025  -  9]</p><p>= 24128</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that,</p><p>Sum of cube of first n numbers = [n(n+1)/2]<sup>2</sup></p><p>6<sup>3</sup> + 8<sup>3</sup> + 10<sup>3</sup> + 12<sup>3</sup> + ... + 20<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 2<sup>3</sup> * (3<sup>3</sup> + 4<sup>3</sup> + 5<sup>3</sup> + .. + 10<sup>3</sup>)</p><p>= 8 * [(1<sup>3</sup> + 2<sup>3</sup> + 3<sup>3</sup> + .. + 10<sup>3</sup>)  -  (1<sup>3</sup> + 2<sup>3</sup>)]</p><p>= 8 * [(10 * 11/2)<sup>2</sup>  -  (2 * 3/2)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= 8 * [3025  -  9]</p><p>= 24128</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the sum of first 15 terms of the following series?</p><p>1 * 3 + 2 * 4 + 3 * 5 + 4 * 6 + .. + 15<sup>th</sup> term</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2358;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; 15 &#2346;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>1 * 3 + 2 * 4 + 3 * 5 + 4 * 6 + .. + 15&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2346;&#2342;</p>", "options_en": ["1440", "1480", "1460", "1380"], "options_hi": ["1440", "1480", "1460", "1380"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>1 * 3 + 2 * 4 + 3 * 5 + 4 * 6 + .. + 15<sup>th</sup> term</p><p>T<sub>n</sub> = n(n + 2)</p><p><img width=252 height=195 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19497/image008.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>1 * 3 + 2 * 4 + 3 * 5 + 4 * 6 + .. + 15<sup>th</sup> term</p><p>T<sub>n</sub> = n(n + 2)</p><p><img width=252 height=195 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19497/image008.png\"></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p><span>How many whole numbers are there between 244 and 332 which are exactly divisible by 7?</span></p>", "q_hi": "<p>244 &#2324;&#2352; 332 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2320;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2379; 7 &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2340;&#2307; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["20", "27", "13", "7"], "options_hi": ["20", "27", "13", "7"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>\"</p><p>245, 252 &#8230;&#8230;. 329&nbsp;</p><p>an = a + (n&nbsp;&#8211;1)d</p><p>329 = 245 + (n&nbsp;&#8211; 1)7</p><p>329 = 245 + 7n&nbsp;&#8211; 7&nbsp;</p><p>91 = 7n</p><p>n&nbsp;= 13</p><p>There are 13 numbers divisible 7 between 244 and 332.\"</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>\"</p><p>245, 252 &#8230;&#8230;. 329&nbsp;</p><p>an = a + (n&nbsp;&#8211;1)d</p><p>329 = 245 + (n&nbsp;&#8211; 1)7</p><p>329 = 245 + 7n&nbsp;&#8211; 7&nbsp;</p><p>91 = 7n</p><p>n&nbsp;= 13</p><p>There are 13 numbers divisible 7 between 244 and 332.\"</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The 8<sup>th</sup> &#160;term of an arithmetic progression is -17 and 17<sup>th</sup> &#160;term is -71, find the 13<sup>th</sup> &#160;term?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 8&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2346;&#2342; -17 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 17&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2346;&#2342; -71 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 13&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2346;&#2342; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#8211;41", "&#8211;35", "&#8211;47", "&#8211;29"], "options_hi": ["- 41", "- 35", "- 47", "- 29"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "\"<p> N <sup>th</sup> &#160;of an AP = a + (n &#8211; 1)d where a is first term and d is common difference</p><p>&#8211;17 = a + (8 &#8211; 1)d</p><p>&#8211;71 = a + (17 &#8211; 1)d</p><p>From above equations we get a = 25 and d = &#8211;6</p><p> 13 <sup>th&#160;</sup> term = 25 + (13 &#8211; 1)( - 6) = &#8211;47</p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> N <sup>th</sup> &#160;of an AP = a + (n &#8211; 1)d where a is first term and d is common difference</p><p>&#8211;17 = a + (8 &#8211; 1)d</p><p>&#8211;71 = a + (17 &#8211; 1)d</p><p>From above equations we get a = 25 and d = &#8211;6</p><p> 13 <sup>th&#160;</sup> term = 25 + (13 &#8211; 1)( - 6) = &#8211;47</p>\""}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of N, if N = 5 + 55 + 555 + .... + 55555555.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; N = 5 + 55 + 555 + .... + 55555555 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; N &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["61728390", "61548770", "61296130", "61997230"], "options_hi": ["61728390", "61548770", "61296130", "61997230"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>N = 5 + 55 + 555 + .... + 55555555</p><p>N = 5 * (1 + 11 + 111 + .... + 11111111)</p><p>N = 5 * (12345678)</p><p><b>N = 61728390</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>N = 5 + 55 + 555 + .... + 55555555</p><p>N = 5 * (1 + 11 + 111 + .... + 11111111)</p><p>N = 5 * (12345678)</p><p><b>N = 61728390</b></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many terms of the series -11, -8, -5, ......... must be taken so that the sum of all the terms is 9?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2342; -11, -8, -5, ......... &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2346;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; 9 &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["11", "8", "9", "10"], "options_hi": ["11", "8", "9", "10"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Series given = -11, -8, -5, .........</p><p>Sum of the series = 9</p><p>Let n number of terms be taken.</p><p>By the formula of arithmetic progression,</p><p>9 = n/2 [2 * -11 + (n  -  1) * 3]</p><p>9 = (n/2) [-22 + 3n  -  3]</p><p>18 = 3n<sup>2</sup>  -  25n</p><p>3n<sup>2</sup>  -  25n  -  18 = 0</p><p>3n<sup>2</sup>  -  27n + 2n  -  18 = 0</p><p>3n (n  -  9) + 2 (n  -  9) = 0</p><p>(n  -  9) (3n + 2) = 0</p><p>n = 9 or -2/3 [n cannot be negative]</p><p>So, n = 9</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Series given = -11, -8, -5, .........</p><p>Sum of the series = 9</p><p>Let n number of terms be taken.</p><p>By the formula of arithmetic progression,</p><p>9 = n/2 [2 * -11 + (n  -  1) * 3]</p><p>9 = (n/2) [-22 + 3n  -  3]</p><p>18 = 3n<sup>2</sup>  -  25n</p><p>3n<sup>2</sup>  -  25n  -  18 = 0</p><p>3n<sup>2</sup>  -  27n + 2n  -  18 = 0</p><p>3n (n  -  9) + 2 (n  -  9) = 0</p><p>(n  -  9) (3n + 2) = 0</p><p>n = 9 or -2/3 [n cannot be negative]</p><p>So, n = 9</p>"}]}